A||||32||Formula||4'x10" dash speakers for cheap at.....||||1||
Z||000000||Formula||12-19-1999||02:40 PM||||there are 4"x10" dash speakers that sound really nice at radio shack for $14 a piece. I give them 2 thumbs up for sound to price ratio. anyway................<BR>has anybody replaced the 4 x 6 speakers in the back. I was looking at it and it seems that it could be a lot of work for "not a big improvement". those were only $9.<P>do you have to take that whole grey plastic piece out or does the grill pop out. (4x6s).<P><BR>This is a little bit off-topic, but do you think a fiero would look good in red, with white stripes and Tom's headlight upgrade?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bill Osmer||12-19-1999||04:32 PM||||In order to change the rear speakers (in the "B" pillar), you have to remove the entire grey plastic piece (AKA trim).||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||12-19-1999||06:27 PM||||We've talked about speakers here before.  The Radio Shack speakers might be cheap, but the best you'll get from them will be factory sound.  Personally, I don't want factory sound.  That's why I upgraded to a much better speaker that will last longer.  You don't have to spend a ton of money to upgrade your stereos sound.  You can get good speakers for around $80/pair.  So for $160, you'll have new speakers.  You'll be amazed at the difference.  And you can get some great deals on aftermarket stereos, too.  Don't be intimidated by some of these systems that cost well over $1000 and include multiple amps and subs, etc.  A good aftermarket CD player can be had for as little as $150.  So, for around $300, you can vastly improve the sound quality.  I've gotten quite long winded, haven't I? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Just my opinion.||||reg||1
Z||000003||CUTTER||12-19-1999||08:48 PM||||I am getting kenwood 4x10's and eclipse 4x6's and they sound great. The kenwoods are $99.99 and the eclipse's are $89.00. Also, I just riped my covers right off the 4x6's. As long as you do it carefully you might be able to get all 4 clips out without breaking them. I broke 1 of the 4 on the one side and none on the other side. Just dont know if they go back in.||||reg||1
Z||000004||overlord||12-19-1999||09:12 PM||||i just bought a cd player along with some kenwood 4*10's.<P>they sound pretty good...160 watts for 120 canadian.||||reg||1
Z||000005||BluByYou||12-20-1999||07:50 AM||||Stereos and fieros .... the neverending question.  I agree that your Radio Shack price-point is going to give you factory sound at best.  Personally, I have an Alpine CD unit, Kicker front speakers and Boston Acoustic rear speakers - maybe $550 in it.  It's not a killer system, but vastly better than original.  I removed the entire trim piece to replace my 4x6 speakers.  Nothing broken, nothing to fix.  Sure it takes more time, but I like to keep my car in good shape.  Regarding the stripe question .... I have an '87 GT - was originally blue over gray.  I had the bottom gray repainted and color-matched to the blue, had twin 7" white stripes put on, then sprayed the gray centers of the wheels white.  Does it look good?  I need to get some pics posted for you to be the judge.  All I can say is that it turns heads, but maybe it's a local thing (?).  Anyway, I sure do like it.||||reg||6
Z||000006||DJRice||12-20-1999||10:05 AM||||Pioneer 4x10s: $80<BR>Pioneer 4x6s: $75<BR>Sony In-Dash CD Player: $200<P>Rolling down the Highway during a mild Fall (mid 70s with the bright blue sky) on Florida's Space Coast with the wind in your face and Fiero's system Kickin: <B>Priceless!</B><P>Some things money can't buy, for everything else you'll have to fire up the Pontiac!<p>[This message has been edited by DJRice (edited 12-20-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero56||12-20-1999||10:13 AM||||And don't forget your Visa card, 'cause the Fiero Store don't take American Express.||||reg||6
Z||000008||Monkeyman||12-20-1999||12:59 PM||||BluByYou--Where in Indiana are you from?  I'm from Wabash.  I don't know about anybody else, but I'd like to see some pics of your car.  And I'd like to hear about anybodys' stereos.  I've gotten some good ideas from some of the members already, but I'm getting my '85 GT next month and I need the tunes.||||reg||1
Z||000009||BluByYou||12-20-1999||02:02 PM||||Hey Monkeyman!  Nice to know a fellow Fiero online guy who's so close.  I'm up in Auburn, along with several other Fieros.  The stereo question is one that could be addressed for hours.  A person can do sub-tubes behind the seats, stock subwoofer, disc-changer .... yada yada yada.  The question always comes back to what YOU like.  Personally, a strong head unit and good speakers were enough for me.  I've had subs, amps, eq's, component speakers and all that jazz in other cars, but for a Fiero - a good set of tunes and a GREAT ride is cool for me.  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||BENGAL4||12-20-1999||02:12 PM||||Formula,<P>Take out the entire plastic piece. You will need a Torx socket to remove the seat belt bolt. Do not try to remove the speaker cover. You will more than likley break one of the posts that hold it in. ALA Monkeyman, this I know from experience. When I redid my interior, I had to go to a boneyard to get a replacement panel.||||reg||1
Z||000011||CUTTER||12-20-1999||03:33 PM||||I broke one of my things off of the cover for the 4x6. will I still be able to put it back on? If I have to I will superglue it till the mean time when I find a replacement!||||reg||1
Z||000012||Formula||12-20-1999||03:52 PM||||I have a sony explode 10" sub for bass, and I have the "cheap" radio shack speakers up front and factorys in the back. I think that the radio shack speakers are good enough because they don't need to handle many watts. To my ears, a tweeter is a tweeter, and thats all that they are being used as.<BR>Before I couldn't turn the cd player to the front  (blown) speakers and I only used the rear.<P> I will refrase my orginal comment and say "Having all 4 speakers sounds nice!".<P> For those of you non to mid end stereo users the radio shacks will work 10x better then an 11 to 16 year old factory speaker. But to high end users like some people here, they prefer the $80 speakers.<P>Monkeyman in 2004!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000013||Steven||12-22-1999||06:34 PM||||I like the after-market speakers for the sound they put out and the fact the when your done the car still looks factory. Radios on the other had never have the good clean fit of the factory. Now I bought the AM/FM Stereo w/CD player and 9 band grapic eq. that Pontiac puts into most of their cars now (i.e. Grand Am, Grand Prix ect.) and it looks and sounds better than the orginal radio. $330 and I am happy.||||reg||5
Z||000014||Richard Parnell||12-22-1999||07:39 PM||||Fiero Store does too take Merkin Express!||||reg||6
Z||000015||Monkeyman||12-22-1999||11:03 PM||||Steven--There are at least a couple of good, name brand stereos that are the 1.5 DIN size meaning they fit GM/Chrysler exactly.  They are a little expensive, but if you want an aftermarket stereo while keeping the fit, that's the way to go.  Also, check out batboys site.  He's got one in the Batmobile.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Steven||12-23-1999||12:35 PM||||Thanks Monkeyman! I will have to look. I do have a question though. Part of what I like about the factory radios is that Pontiac lights up orange. Do you know of any aftermarket radios that light up orange. Now I know that this sounds petty, but I drive a lot at night and that is one of my little pet peaves. Maybe it is time for me to take my medacine?||||reg||10
Z||000017||BluByYou||12-23-1999||01:45 PM||||Steven:  I hear what you're saying about the lighting.  I tried to find the reddish/orange lighting too.  The audiophile I was dealing with looked at me as if I'd just fallen off the turnip truck and landed on my head.  I once had a Blaupunkt Denver that you could switch the lights from green to orange.  The switch was right there on the front - if your mood changed, hit the button.  No problem.  Blaupunkt makes a decent CD player, but mine went a little sour after about three years.  Started having electronic problems with it.||||reg||1
Z||000018||DRH||12-23-1999||02:50 PM||||Steven, I'm with you. I want a radio that matches the interior (including lights). Where did you get yours? I've ask a couple of boneyards and they said the nicer radios are usually gone before they get the car. I assumed a dealer would be very pricey but have not looked yet.<P>David.||||reg||1
Z||000019||RossT||12-23-1999||11:20 PM||||steven, what kind of modifications did you have to do, to get the wiring harness to fit.<BR>I understand that the newer gm units do not<BR>connect to the older wiring harness.<BR>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000020||AL||12-24-1999||02:25 AM|||| I AGREE WITH FORMULA,i bought 51/2 inch for my sub and it works great and for 16 bucks why not,if your like me i like to play good old fashioned rock and roll, i like to here every instrument and not just the bass kickin in your head.radio shack rules!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000021||Voyd||12-24-1999||03:15 AM||||go check out crutchfield.com. certain high end Sony's and Kenwoods have red illumination. ||||reg||1
Z||000022||batboy||12-24-1999||08:14 AM||||Seems like most CD car players nowadays have multi-colored displays. My old Kenwood in my 85 GT is switchable from light red to green, but they don't make that model anymore. I saw several CD players that had mostly pink or red displays in Crutchfield's catalog. Pioneer, Sony, Panasonic, and Clarion. Seems like blue illumination is becoming very popular in car stereos now too.||||reg||1
Z||000023||Phaeton||12-25-1999||05:22 PM||||The local chevy dealer has an adapter to put their new radios into their older cars.  I put GM cd in and the adapter was foolproof, just wish I had thought about the illumination color before I bought.||||reg||1
Z||000024||Raydar||12-26-1999||12:02 AM||||Check this out... <A HREF="http://www.aatechnologies.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.aatechnologies.com/</A> <BR>They have various years of Pontiac (and other GM) radios. Also, I was in Hi-Fi Buys last week. Alpine now has a 1.5 DIN CD unit that looks really nice. Pioneer and Jensen have had 1.5 DIN radios for a while.||||reg||1
Z||000025||batboy||12-26-1999||08:10 AM||||As the GM size aftermarket stereos become more popular and more models are produced, the price will significantly come down. My DEH-45 Pioneer CD player was only $40 to $50 more than most of the other DIN low end decks. The Jensens are cheaper yet, but maybe not as good. With more competition, the price will soon drop down to about the same as the regular stereos, mark my words.<P>Cutter, way back up in the thread you asked it a broken rear grill tab could be repaired. I broke one off of my 87 SE before I realized that the whole panel had to be removed. Seems like half the people with Fieros do this too.<P>When the trim panel was still out, I glued the grill back in place using that "Shoe Goo" adhesive that you can buy in K-Mart or Wal-Mart in the sports department. I've used Shoe Goo for years. Actually it doesn't work as well on shoes as advertised, but it's amazing stuff on most other things around the house and on interior car things. It works really great on plastic, wood, and vinyl. No, I don't own any stock in the company. With a supply Shoe Goo and Duct Tape around, you can fix just about anything.||||reg||1
Z||000026||Monkeyman||12-26-1999||07:26 PM||||batboy--I just marked your words like you said and now I can't get the magic marker off of my monitor screen!  Thanks!  Now what do I do, huh?!  I think you owe me a new monitor!  (BTW-I saw a real nice one the other day.  21" LCD.  Only a couple thousand bucks.  I'll be looking for it in the mail! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<P>Kenwood makes a good CD player in their "eXceleron" (or something like that) line that has a red display.  There is also a company in NY (I think) that can change the color of your current display.  (Now, if I can just find their name...)||||reg||1
